 "description": "FRAME GENERATION COST BY PICTURE PRESET: 1.3's sizing (the stream sized by the bitrate, as 1.3.11 compiled it), 1888x1696 per eye with its foveation, as the launcher compiles it for the Vision Pro (harness/density_check.py's case: sliders 0.80 / 0.90, the quality window; centre 0.946 x 0.888, shift 1.0 / 0.183, edge 3.2 / 4.0). Generation at half rate, host 90 Hz, the app free between 50 and 70 fps (held to 45), the mock headset's display emulation. The four e2e_fg_size_* runs compare what generation costs and whether it holds the display rate as the preset grows (1.4: users saw generation slow down): the generator renders every output at the full side-by-side frame before the foveation, and with generation on the encoder encodes every display slot. harness/fg_size_report.py puts the four side by side (game, encoder, generator).",
